course: dictionary
lesson: 10896
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. «A VR (virtual reality) headset makes the brain feel somewhere else; the experience is real, but your body stays in the room.» The words VR and headset are your clues: virtual here means made by a computer, not in the real physical world.
explain: Virtual also means almost completely, though not officially. «A virtual stranger» is someone you hardly know. Read the words around virtual to see which meaning fits, then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: In science, virtual has a special meaning. In a flat mirror, the image you see seems to be behind the glass, but it cannot be shown on a screen. That is a virtual image.
fact: Virtual means made or seen on a computer or online, not in the real physical world.
fact: «Virtual reality» (VR) is a computer-made experience that makes you feel you are somewhere else.
fact: Virtual can also mean almost completely, as in «a virtual certainty», which means almost certain.
fact: A virtual image seems to be behind a mirror or lens, but it cannot be shown on a screen.
fact: Phrases to know: virtual classroom, virtual tour, virtual pet, virtual stranger.
exercise: «A VR (virtual reality) headset makes the brain feel somewhere else.» What does virtual mean here? | Really happening in front of you | A kind of metal | *Made by a computer, not in the real world | Very old
exercise: Ella takes a virtual tour of a museum from her bedroom on her tablet. What does virtual mean here? | Very quick | Painted on a wall | *Seen online, not in the real place | Walking through the real museum
exercise: Dad says Mr Brown is a virtual stranger, because he has only met him once. What does virtual mean? | A stranger who is a computer | A close friend | Completely unknown forever | *Almost a stranger, hardly known
test: «Rain is a virtual certainty today, so bring a coat.» What does virtual mean? | *Almost completely, nearly certain | Not sure at all | Made by a computer | Happening in a mirror
test: In a flat mirror you see a virtual image of yourself. What is a virtual image? | A very bright light | Painted on the glass | Printed on paper | *An image that seems to be behind the mirror and cannot be shown on a screen
exam: Which sentence uses virtual to mean online or made by a computer? | *Our virtual lesson started at nine o'clock on the laptop | The sky is virtual and grey today | The jumper is a virtual match for my trousers | He is a virtual giant of a man
